{"author":{"id":"f4e4dbe251fbd7519eab696986bae317e93a786739d6cebe9c4c1e89dd44e465"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793681970,"nonce":"n0JJ12N/PPiVBqbnYBNG2d9gW7c=","title":"BundleTests edits the tracked lean/bundle-roots.txt in place","message":"Found by the M4 code review (adversarial reviewer). Listed under \"Not addressed here\" in https://github.com/icosahedron/csharp-ansatz/pull/1. Parent epic: `54c6e06f383039f9758f1571999c683db1c244561561998cf9a52c41b84fa52f`.\n\n`BundleTests.TheExportScriptFailsOnAMissingRoot` adds a missing root to `lean/bundle-roots.txt` to check that `scripts/export-semantics.sh` fails, then restores the file in a `finally` block. A test run that is killed while the script runs leaves the tracked root list modified. The next bundle export then fails, or worse, exports with a wrong root if the change goes unnoticed.\n\nFix: have the script take the roots file as a parameter, or through an environment variable that defaults to `lean/bundle-roots.txt`. The test can then pass a temporary copy and never touch the tracked file.","files":null}]}